Track 2: Al-Qamar’s Calibration
- Story & Context: In the darkened tent of Al-Qamar, the local tinkerer whispered the secret of the salvaged synthesizers, admitting that the machines only sing when fed the static of a dying star. I sat on a woven rug, feeling the sub-bass rattle the loose coins in my pocket as he confessed his fear of the silence that follows the power cut. "Find the frequency where the copper screams and the sand holds its breath."
