- Story & Context: Years after the great caravan dispersal, the myth of the six-minute song persists, a track supposedly recorded on a loop that captures the exact moment the world stops spinning. Travelers still gather at the site of the vanished market, staring at their empty wrists as if waiting for an appointment that was canceled decades ago. "We are only the shadows of the time we failed to keep."
